# The negation of a ball with a 2-limb center: exact, the radius unchanged.
kernel:        ball_neg_2
input:         cx = cx0 cx1
input:         stored rx
output:        cz = cz0 cz1
output:        rz
value:         -cx
requires:      ball cx rx
ensures:       normalized cz
ensures:       encloses cz rz -x x=cx,rx
min_precision: 1
theorem:       proofs/theories/Ball.v ball_neg_2_correct
source:        midpoint-radius negation (Milestone 1 listing)
license:       algorithm and proof: MIT
status:        proved
domain:        extended
ieee_status:   unverified
entry:         yes
cone_exempt:   the radius never reaches the center; the special states of the ball layer (Milestone 1 statements, Ball kernels) test the center and the radii

(cz0, cz1) = neg_2(cx0, cx1)
rz         = copy(rx)
